From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:52:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10558/11362] Wire generator provenance into every eval row
 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6790)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The helpers landed inert in 8b968753dd. This commit lands the deferred
call site. `run_game` now snapshots the proposer's completion counters
around the game loop and emits `generator_provenance`,
`completions_consumed`, and `llm_reached` on every per-game row. A row
with `completions_consumed == 0` now says plainly that no model was
reached, which the 22-hour nine-game run of 2026-08-31 could not say.

The self-failing placeholder test is replaced by
`test_run_game_rows_carry_generator_provenance_fields`. It restores the
five displaced assertions plus a sixth: mutation testing showed that
substituting `_gen_prov = generator_provenance(policy)` with a constant
left the suite green under the original five. With the sixth, all 8
mutations (5 deletions, 3 constant substitutions) go RED.

Three freshness-lint artifacts are rebuilt with their recorded rebuild
commands; the deep diffs moved ONLY bookkeeping:
- outer_loop_arc_gateway_rescore_20260726: 17 fields (dates, heads,
  dep shas, duration, checksum, peer-artifact sha). Zero measurements.
- outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore_20260726: 13 fields, same
  classes. Zero measurements.
- outer_loop_arc_max_actions_answer_20260726: 7 fields, matching the
  precedent rebuild. ANSWER unchanged (central=4000 conservative=2000).

Two queued rebuilds were NOT committed, deliberately. The
arc_gateway_card_ground_truth_20260727 rebuild is a live 48-cell re-run
and it moves MEASURED values (23/48 cells reproduce July trajectories;
model-wrong 17->19 of 44; REAL median optimism 0.018097->0.02481). An
A/B control with the wiring reverted produced identical measured values,
so the movement is prior arc_competition_agent.py drift, not this
change. The per-level capture's own pure-addition proof reports 79
number-bearing diffs for the same reason. Those corrections belong to
the agent change stream with their own review. Full record appended to
ops/known-issues.md (2026-08-31 entry).

Rejected alternative: acknowledging the drift via
freshness_acknowledgements instead of rebuilding — rebuilding proves
inertness by construction where it is true, and surfaces the drift
where it is not.

